---

## API Authentication

The Lament API uses **Master Key** authentication. All non-public endpoints require the `X-Master-Key` or `x-api-key` header.

### Public Endpoints (No Auth)

These paths are accessible without authentication:

- `GET /` — API info
- `GET /health` — Health check
- `GET /ping` — Ping
- `GET /maintenance` — Maintenance status
- `GET /stream/*` — Audio streaming
- `GET /images/*` — Image serving

### Protected Endpoints

All other endpoints require authentication:

```bash
curl -H "X-Master-Key: your_master_key" \
  https://api.lament.rynds.my.id/tracks
```

### Master-Only Endpoints

Some endpoints require master-level access (via `MasterOnly` middleware):

- Client management (`/clients`)
- Playlist management (`/playlists`)
- Music upload (`POST /music`)
- Image refresh (`/refresh-image/*`)

## Frontend Proxy Authentication

The SvelteKit frontend injects the API key server-side. The browser never sees the master key:

```
Browser → SvelteKit Server → [Injects X-Master-Key] → Hono API
```

## Client API Keys

The `clients` table stores API keys with:
- `key_hash` — Bcrypt-hashed API key
- `is_active` — Whether the key is enabled
- `name` — Client name
- `contact` — Contact information
